erent in terms  of what should the country be willing to  do and by the country I mean people with  our tax money in terms of how that tax  money is allocated to deal with poverty  to deal with hunger and in order to  really do that we have to understand the  destructive effect that poverty has  kids in their ability to do well in life  and you can pick celebrities or athletes  who were dealt a bad hand and did really  well they are statistically irrelevant I  don't mean I don't care about them but I  mean statistically that is not even  really an important part of the mobility  conversation that we need to be having  and that's really the issue that we  should be talking about here but a gaffe  no question about it evidence that Biden  is inherently racist certainly not by  itself but very very much hitting on an  important issue that even though poor  kids and wealthy kids may have the same  potential at least in some hypothetical  sense the reality of poverty is  absolutely crushing
 

